+|rtx.atmosphere.numos.timeOfDayHours|float|12|0|24|The time of day in hours, from 0 to 24\. 12 is solar noon\. Around an equinox, 6 is about sunrise and 18 about sunset\. While the time cycle runs, this is the start time, and editing it moves the clock\. While the cycle is off it still places the sun, so it works as a manual time\-of\-day control\.|
+|rtx.atmosphere.numos.unitsPerMeter|float|0|0||How many game units make one real meter\. This measures the game and is not a look setting: for example 100 for an engine that works in centimeters, or 39\.37 for one that works in inches\. 0 takes the value from rtx\.sceneScale\. The clouds, sky, haze, fog, local\-light glow and lightning all convert with it\. To make the sky smaller than the game's real scale, change World Scale and leave this at the true value\.|
+|rtx.atmosphere.numos.useCameraWorldOverride|bool|False|||Anchors the clouds to rtx\.atmosphere\.numos\.cameraWorldOverride instead of the camera position the renderer sees\. Turn it on for games that render relative to the camera, where the camera always appears to sit at the origin and the clouds would otherwise move with the view\. The game integration then has to send the real camera position every frame\.|
+|rtx.atmosphere.numos.weather.followGame|bool|True|||Enables showing the preset that is bound to the weather the game reports in rtx\.atmosphere\.numos\.weather\.gameWeather\. The sky shows only rtx\.atmosphere\.numos\.weather\.preset when this is off\.|
