+|rtx.atmosphere.numos.worldScale|float|1|0.001|1000|The size of the sky's world relative to the game's\. The planet, atmosphere, clouds, wind and lightning are all scaled by it together, so a scaled sky looks like the full\-size one, only smaller\. The haze, fog and local\-light glow follow Haze World Scale instead\. 1 is real size\. Lower it for a map built much smaller than the place it depicts, where real\-size clouds look too high and too large \(0\.1 makes the sky a tenth of the size\)\.<br>Settings given in meters or kilometers \(cloud heights and depths, the lightning range\) scale with it\. Settings in world units \(Ground Level, Cloud Vertical Offset, Camera World Override\) are the game's own units and do not\.|
