+# Enhanced sky options
+
+Game integrations select the Enhanced sky through `SetConfigVariable("rtx.skyMode", "2")`. Mode 0 renders the
+game's sky and mode 1 renders the Standard atmosphere. A live VR session interprets 2 as 1 on the device,
+including its desktop view. Ending the session makes the requested Enhanced sky available again.
+
+All 221 live library settings use `rtx.atmosphere.numos.` followed by the library suffix. For example,
+`rtx.atmosphere.numos.cloudDensity` defaults to 20 per kilometre, and `rtx.atmosphere.numos.moon2.phase`
+addresses the third configurable moon. Quality levels 0, 1 and 2 select High, Medium and Low.
+`rtx.volumetrics.enable` takes precedence over Enhanced aerial perspective and height fog.
+
+| Additional option below `rtx.atmosphere.numos.` | Use |
+|---|---|
+| `worldChangeCount` | Change the counter when the map or world changes to invalidate ground measurements. |
+| `cloudMotionVectors` | Use the cloud's depth and motion where it covers a surface. |
+| `cloudMotionVectorCoverage` | Opacity threshold for choosing the cloud depth. |
+| `weather.preset` | Manual built-in name. An empty name uses the current numeric sky settings. |
+| `weather.followGame` | Allow a recognized game weather to take priority over the manual preset. |
+| `weather.gameWeather` | First built-in name recognized in the comma-separated list. Names are case-insensitive. |
+| `weather.gameWeatherOutgoing` | Outgoing game's weather for an explicitly controlled blend. |
+| `weather.gameWeatherBlend` | Blend from outgoing to incoming over 0–1. A negative value uses the timed transition. |
+| `weather.transitionSeconds` | Duration of automatic transitions. Zero switches immediately. |
+
+Built-in names are `Clear`, `Fair`, `PartlyCloudy`, `Cloudy`, `Overcast`, `Haze`, `Fog`, `Storm`, `Drizzle`,
+`Altostratus` and `Cirrus`. A preset supplies the fields the library defines for that weather. Other fields
+come from the current numeric settings. For fully custom weather, clear `weather.preset` and `weather.gameWeather`
+and set the numeric fields. All selection and blending take place in memory.
+
+[RtxOptions.md](../RtxOptions.md) lists every key, type, default and limit.
+[NumosSky.md](../documentation/NumosSky.md) describes rendering and the files to ship.
